 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for committed changes.** Fast updates and independence from a realtime provider justify owning connection capacity and reconnect operations. Five-second HTTPS polling would simplify stateless operations but add repeated reads and several seconds of lag; a hosted realtime service would reduce connection operations but introduce recurring fees and provider coupling. Both alternatives can meet the freshness goal. See [Board Change Delivery](decisions/board-change-delivery.md) for the comparison.
